{"name":"Leprechaun","hex":"#29906d","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"leprechaun","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A type of diminutive, solitary fairy or sprite, traditionally depicted as a small, bearded man wearing a green coat and hat, often found repairing a single shoe; they typically possess hidden treasure, such as a pot of gold hidden at the end of a rainbow, and can be forced to reveal its location if captured.","An Irish person."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/leprechaun"}],"entries":[{"title":"Leprechaun","blocks":[{"text":"A leprechaun is a diminutive supernatural being in Irish folklore, classed by some as a type of solitary fairy. They are usually depicted as little bearded men, wearing a coat and hat, who partake in mischief. In later times, they have been depicted as shoe-makers who have a hidden pot of gold at the end of the rainbow."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0b/Leprechaun_ill_artlibre_jnl.png/330px-Leprechaun_ill_artlibre_jnl.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Leprechaun","wikidata":"Q244392"},{"title":"Leprechaun (film series)","blocks":[{"text":"Leprechaun is an American horror comedy film series consisting of eight films. Beginning with Leprechaun (1993), the series centers on a malevolent and murderous leprechaun who resorts to any means necessary to protect and reclaim his gold. Warwick Davis plays the title role in every film except for the 2014 film Leprechaun: Origins, and the 2018 film Leprechaun Returns, in which the character is portrayed by Dylan Postl and Linden Porco, respectively."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/d/d4/LepPotofGore.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Leprechaun_(film_series)","wikidata":"Q1763934"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/